# Root module: design tokens only.
#
# This file used to also re-register every service and settings singleton that
# services/qmldir and Settings/qmldir already register. In QML a singleton
# registered by two different modules is two *distinct types with separate
# instances*, so a file resolving CenterState through the root import got a
# different object -- with different state -- from one resolving it through
# "services". Which one you got depended on the order of the import statements
# at the top of each file, so adding or reordering an import could silently
# split the shell's state in half.
#
# Services are registered in exactly one place: services/qmldir.
# Settings likewise in Settings/qmldir.
singleton Colors Colors.qml
singleton Theme Theme.qml
